{{- /*
product_relations.gohtml edits a product's related products (ADR 0181).

Each kind is a textarea holding one handle per line, in the order the storefront
shows them. A handle is what an operator knows; a picker over the whole catalog
would not fit a catalog of fifty thousand products. The form is POSTed inside
the panel tree for the reason product_edit.gohtml's is.

All three lists are saved together, and a list the module refuses leaves all
three as they were: the form comes back with what was typed and the module's
sentence naming the line to fix.
*/ -}}
{{ define "body" }}
<p><a href="{{ .CancelPath }}">← Back to the product</a></p>

<h1>Related products of {{ .Product.Title }}</h1>
{{ if .Error }}<p role="alert">{{ .Error }}</p>{{ end }}

<form method="post" action="{{ .ActionPath }}">
  {{ range .Lists }}
  <label>{{ .Label }} ({{ .Kind }})
    <textarea name="{{ .Kind }}" rows="6">{{ .Text }}</textarea>
  </label>
  {{ end }}
  <p>One product per line, by its handle or its id, in the order the storefront
  shows them; at most {{ .Limit }} in each list. A draft, or a product sold in
  another channel, can be listed: the storefront leaves it out until it can
  show it. An empty list takes that kind off.</p>
  <button type="submit">Save</button>
  <a href="{{ .CancelPath }}">Cancel</a>
</form>
{{ end }}
